# netsurf: floats a script inserts or removes among blocks placed locally (patch 365)
# Generated 2026-11-01
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 364)
#
# A float between blocks is an anonymous inline container (a "float
# carrier") holding a float box that wraps the element's box
# (box_construct.c). The local block path (166/176) knew nothing of that:
#  - in a container holding only blocks, a script-inserted float WAS
#    built locally, but box_construct puts its carrier at the END of the
#    parent, and the path laid the page out with it there: the float drew
#    below the last block (one insert: 120 rows off the static render;
#    "full layout (new block not in its parent)") -- a correctness bug;
#  - once a carrier was among the children, every later insert or
#    removal there was a full box-tree rebuild ("parent holds more than
#    blocks"): 220-270 ms on a 2500-paragraph page.
#
#  - html.c: html_rl_float_carrier() recognises a carrier (only float
#    boxes, each wrapping one element box). html_rl_block_change accepts
#    carriers among the children (a float whose element left is
#    removed, its carrier freed when emptied) and a float's element box
#    under them; a new float is taken out of wherever the builder put it
#    and placed in DOM order -- after the previous sibling's float in its
#    carrier, first in the carrier of the floats after it, or in a new
#    carrier after the previous sibling's box. The "after" search climbs
#    from a sibling's box to its box under the parent
#    (html_rl_top_under), so a block inserted after a float lands after
#    the carrier, not before it. Floats present: the page is laid out
#    once ("full layout (a float among the blocks)" / "(floats among the
#    blocks)"). A container whose first child is a carrier now reaches
#    the block path too. The sibling-combinator check reads a removed
#    float's element and floats' elements as neighbours
#    (html_rl_removed_nodes; a carrier has no node).
#
# Result: 220 -> 21 ms (median, 2500-paragraph page), and the float in
# its place. Gate: JS-float-insert-one and JS-float-insert (eight
# inserts, moves and a removal) render row for row as the same DOM
# written statically; every intermediate state of the eight was checked
# the same way against a parse-time build (0 rows each).
#
